import Mathlib.Tactic
import InfoGeometry.Canonical.ProjectiveFoundation

/-!
# Klein Bottle Monodromy Representation

This module defines the algebraic signature for the monodromy representation of 
the fundamental group of the Klein bottle into the projective linear group.

The Klein bottle is a non-orientable solvmanifold, whose fundamental group $\pi_1(K)$
is generated by an orientation-reversing glide $a$ and a translation $b$, subject 
to the defining relation:
$$ a b a^{-1} b = 1 $$

When evaluating the isomonodromic deformations (Painlevé VI) of a $2 \times 2$ 
Fuchsian system on this manifold, the monodromy matrices must satisfy this relation 
projectively. This introduces a central scalar "twist" $\{\pm I\}$ that neutralizes 
the chiral anomaly, locking the eigenvalues and stabilizing the deformation.
-/

namespace InfoGeometry.Topology.KleinMonodromy

open InfoGeometry.Canonical.ProjectiveFoundation

variable {K V : Type*} [Field K] [AddCommGroup V] [Module K V]

/-- 
The representation of the Klein bottle fundamental group $\pi_1(K)$ 
into the general linear group $\operatorname{GL}(V)$, up to a central projective twist.

The relation $a b a^{-1} b = \lambda I$ algebraically encodes the non-orientable 
topological identification of the twisted torus.
-/
structure KleinMonodromyRepresentation (K V : Type*) [Field K] [AddCommGroup V] [Module K V] where
  /-- The orientation-reversing loop monodromy matrix. -/
  a : V ≃ₗ[K] V
  
  /-- The parabolic/translational loop monodromy matrix. -/
  b : V ≃ₗ[K] V
  
  /-- The projective central scalar encoding the Möbius twist. -/
  twist : Kˣ
  
  /-- 
  The compatibility relation of the Klein bottle fundamental group.
  The sequence of operations mathematically refocuses the diffusion:
  $a \cdot b \cdot a^{-1} \cdot b = \lambda \cdot I$
  -/
  relation : a * b * a⁻¹ * b = twist • (1 : V ≃ₗ[K] V)

end InfoGeometry.Topology.KleinMonodromy
